From f3cf344870ab6b6a23454609f434618733881e16 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: modpunk <27315771+modpunk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 21:20:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Bluetooth: hci_bcm: Add BCM4350 support

The iPhone 6s has the Bluetooth half of a BCM4350 on an Apple S5L UART
with RTS/CTS. It behaves like the BCM4349 (drive RTS while powering up),
which is how it was brought up: the stock driver bound through the
brcm,bcm4349-bt entry loaded the 80 KiB patchram at 115200 baud and the
controller came up with LE scanning working.

Signed-off-by: modpunk <27315771+modpunk@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c
index 9a103db7e355..da4b30e7c00c 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c
@@ -1591,6 +1591,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id bcm_bluetooth_of_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "brcm,bcm43430a1-bt" },
 	{ .compatible = "brcm,bcm43438-bt", .data = &bcm43438_device_data },
 	{ .compatible = "brcm,bcm4349-bt", .data = &bcm43438_device_data },
+	{ .compatible = "brcm,bcm4350-bt", .data = &bcm43438_device_data },
 	{ .compatible = "brcm,bcm43540-bt", .data = &bcm4354_device_data },
 	{ .compatible = "brcm,bcm4335a0" },
 	{ .compatible = "cypress,cyw4373a0-bt", .data = &cyw4373a0_device_data },
